  "prefLabel": "Env-A 609.16 Permit Renewal and Expiration Date Established",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-10-24",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 609.16 Permit Renewal and Expiration Date Established.\n\n(a) Each title V operating permit shall be issued for a period of 5 years and may be renewed in accordance with Env-A 609.18.\n\n(b) The amendment or modification of a title V operating permit shall not affect the permit expiration date contained in the permit.\n\n(c) The acid rain portion of a title V operating permit shall be issued for a period of 5 years and shall be renewed in accordance with Env-A 611.\n\nSource. #6057-B, eff 6-30-95; ss by #7879, eff 4-26-03; ss by #9906, INTERIM, eff 4-26-11, EXPIRES: 10-24-11; ss by #10000, eff 10-1-11; ss by #10175, eff 9-1-12; ss by #13510, eff 12-17-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a600.html"
